 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Where it's decided:** the `MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH` config key, defaulting to `None` (no limit) at `src/tessel/app.py:225`. `Request.max_content_length` in `src/tessel/wrappers.py:60-90` reads it for each request, and a request over the limit gets a 413.\n\n**Per request:** yes. `Request.max_content_length` has a setter (`wrappers.py:88-90`), so a view can set it before touching the body:\n\n```python\nfrom tessel import request\n\n@app.post(\"/upload\")\ndef upload():\n    request.max_content_length = 100 * 1024 * 1024  # this route only\n    f = request.files[\"file\"]\n```\n\nIt has to be set before `request.files`, `request.form`, or `request.get_data()` is first accessed, because the limit is checked when the body is read. `CHANGES.rst:83` notes the per-request override was added deliberately.\n\n`wrappers.py` also has `max_form_memory_size` and `max_form_parts` (around lines 95 and 122). They can raise 413 for `multipart/form-data` too, so check them if the 413 persists.\n\nIf a reverse proxy such as nginx sits in front, its own body-size limit can also return 413 before the request reaches the app.",
